----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. SUB-PRODUCT IDENTIFICATION & POPULATION RULES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO IDENTIFY SUB-PRODUCTS/SIGNING POWERS:

- CRITICAL FILTERING — TWO-GATE TEST:
  A sub-product/power is ONLY eligible for extraction if it PASSES BOTH of the following gates:

  GATE 1 — ELECTRONIC BANKING KEYWORD MATCH:
  The clause must explicitly contain at least one of the following keywords or their direct synonyms:
    • System Administrator(s) / administrators
    • online banking profile
    • subscribe for / subscription to electronic banking
    • electronic banking services / internet banking services
    • electronic banking / electronic platforms
    • E-banking / HSBCnet / H2H / API's
    • Channels / E-Channels (when referring to digital/online delivery channels)
    • authorisation levels (in the context of digital platforms)
    • third parties to manage Channels

  GATE 2 — NOT A GENERAL BANKING POWER:
  Even if Gate 1 keywords appear nearby, REJECT the clause if its PRIMARY action is a general banking
  activity such as:
    • Opening or closing bank accounts
    • Directing provision of banking services (general)
    • Delegating authority in a general/non-digital context
    • Terminating banking relationships
    • Executing general supplemental documents or amendments
  UNLESS the clause EXPLICITLY ties that action to electronic platforms/Channels/E-banking by name.

- A clause that merely mentions "Accounts and E-Channels" in a list alongside general account powers
  should only be extracted if the PRIMARY SUBJECT of the clause is the electronic channel/platform
  itself (e.g., "operate and maintain... E-Channels and use the Services" may qualify;
  "open any account with HSBC" does NOT qualify even if E-Channels appear elsewhere in the document).

- DO NOT extract:
    ✗ "Direct the opening of any account with HSBC and the provision of any services by HSBC"
    ✗ "Further delegate authority, including the power to sub-delegate" (general, not e-banking specific)
    ✗ Any general mandate/signatory powers not tied to digital platforms

- DO extract (examples):
    ✓ "Appoint and revoke System Administrators on HSBCnet"
    ✓ "Make changes to the online banking profile"
    ✓ "Subscribe for electronic banking / E-Channels"
    ✓ "Authorise third parties to manage and/or access the Channels"
    ✓ "Set authorisation levels of administrators on electronic platforms"
    ✓ "Operate and maintain the E-Channels and use the Services" (only if E-Channels is the
       primary subject, not bundled with general account opening)

Step 1 - Link sub-product to account number:
  Apply qualifying Electronic Banking sub-products to the Account Numbers extracted in Section 4.
  Duplicate sub-products for each individual account object if they apply to multiple accounts.

Step 2 - Format Output:
  Each qualifying sub-product gets its own object in the "Sub-Products" array with its own
  "Signing Rule" array.

  If NO sub-products pass both gates, set "Sub-Products": []
